      "claim": "C18 reports an absolute oral bioavailability (Fpod) of 10% in cynomolgus monkeys for compound 4p, below the 20% threshold; the query's ibrutinib-like pyrazolopyrimidine acrylamide structure is consistent with this compound, making this direct low-F evidence if the identity applies.",
      "card_ids": ["C18"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C01 and C05 report low/poor human oral bioavailability for FK3453 attributed to metabolism-mediated clearance, supporting that lipophilic heteroaromatic scaffolds can have F well below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C05"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C12 reports an estimated human absolute oral bioavailability of 3% for astemizole, a lipophilic neutral piperidine, supporting low F for a similar physicochemical profile.",
      "card_ids": ["C12"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C08 reports poor oral bioavailability for danavorexton requiring IV administration, supporting low F for lipophilic small molecules with first-pass or metabolic loss.",
      "card_ids": ["C08"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C22 and C26 report low absolute oral bioavailability in rats for DX-9065 (10.8%) and olcegepant (<1%), respectively, supporting low F for diverse low-solubility molecules.",
      "card_ids": ["C22", "C26"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C16 and C19 report high dog F for FK3453 (71.3%-93.4%), but this is species-specific and does not override the human low-F evidence or the direct low monkey Fpod for compound 4p.",
      "card_ids": ["C16", "C19"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
