      "card_ids": ["C29", "C30", "C31", "C32", "C33", "C34", "C35", "C36", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No human absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query is provided.",
    "C18 reports Fpod for compound 4p in monkeys; the card does not explicitly confirm that compound 4p is the query, so direct applicability is inferred rather than confirmed.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV exposure data for the query are available.",
    "Solubility, permeability, and first-pass metabolism of the query are not directly measured; the prior only indicates unfavorable solubility and mixed/unclear metabolism.",
    "L3 oral exposure records are for other molecules and lack IV comparators or F values, so they are not threshold-relevant for the query.",
    "Species differences in F (e.g., FK3453 high in dogs but low in humans) limit extrapolation from animal data."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is a lipophilic, neutral, heteroaromatic piperidine acrylamide consistent with an ibrutinib-like pyrazolopyrimidine. Direct monkey Fpod of 10% for compound 4p (C18), if applicable, is below the 20% threshold. Transferable low-F contexts (C01/C05, C12, C08) and additional low-F animal records (C22, C26, C28) affirmatively support F < 20%. High dog F for FK3453 (C16/C19) is species-specific and does not overturn the low direction. L3 oral exposure records for other molecules do not provide threshold-relevant F evidence and do not change the decision. Prediction: low."
}

